<article class="env-corollary" id="7F0E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/7F0E">Corollary <span data-tag="7F0E">4.1.2.6</span>.</a> Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be a map of simplicial sets, where $S$ is a Kan complex. Then $p$ is cofinal if and only if it is a weak homotopy equivalence. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Proposition <a href="/tag/7677" data-tag="7677">4.1.2.5</a>, $p$ is cofinal if and only if it is a contravariant equivalence in $(\sSet )_{/S}$. If $S$ is a Kan complex, then Proposition <a href="/tag/79BF" data-tag="79BF">3.1.5.7</a> asserts that the contravariant equivalences are precisely the weak homotopy equivalences. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>